{"timestamp": "2025-11-03T16:38:28.461728", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Simple random policy: keep taking random actions until the episode ends\n  # or a safe step limit is reached.  The function returns the list of\n  # actions that were executed.\n  actions = []\n\n  # Determine the set of possible action IDs.  The environment exposes a\n  # mapping from action names to integer IDs via `action_specs()`.  If that\n  # method is unavailable we fall back to a generic range based on the\n  # attribute `n_actions` (if present) or just use 0\u20114 (the standard DMLab\n  # actions).\n  try:\n      spec = env.action_specs()\n      action_ids = list(spec.values())\n  except Exception:\n      if hasattr(env, \"n_actions\"):\n          action_ids = list(range(env.n_actions))\n      else:\n          # Default to the five basic actions used in CraftWorld\n          action_ids = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]\n\n  # A generous safety bound to avoid infinite loops in pathological cases.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 1000)\n\n  for _ in range(max_steps):\n      # Some environments expose a private `_is_done` helper; otherwise we\n      # rely on the `step` return value.\n      if hasattr(env, \"_is_done\") and callable(env._is_done):\n          if env._is_done():\n              break\n      # Choose a random action and apply it.\n      a = np.random.choice(action_ids)\n      actions.append(int(a))\n      try:\n          reward, done, _ = env.step(a)\n      except Exception:\n          # If the environment follows a different API (e.g., returns\n          # (reward, done, obs) or just (reward, obs)), we ignore the exact\n          # values and rely on the `done` flag when available.\n          done = False\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": -1}}
