{"timestamp": "2025-11-03T16:43:13.912500", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Simple random\u2011action baseline.\n  # Reset the environment to start a new episode and then take random actions\n  # until the task is completed or the maximum number of steps is reached.\n  # The sequence of actions taken is returned as a list of integers.\n  actions = []\n\n  # Reset the environment and obtain the initial observation (not used here).\n  _ = env.reset()\n\n  # Determine the maximum number of steps allowed for the episode.\n  # The CraftLab wrapper stores this as `max_steps`; fall back to a large\n  # default if the attribute is missing.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 1000)\n\n  # Obtain the list of valid action IDs from the environment.\n  action_ids = list(env.action_specs().values())\n\n  for _ in range(max_steps):\n      # If the task is already satisfied, stop early.\n      if env._is_done():\n          break\n\n      # Choose a random action from the available set.\n      action = np.random.choice(action_ids)\n\n      # Execute the action and collect the resulting observation.\n      # The step method returns (reward, done, observation).\n      _reward, done, _obs = env.step(action)\n\n      # Record the action taken.\n      actions.append(int(action))\n\n      # If the environment reports that the episode is done, exit.\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": -1}}
