{"timestamp": "2025-11-03T16:59:50.060966", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Reset the environment to start a new episode and obtain the initial observation\n  obs = env.reset()\n  # List to record the sequence of actions taken\n  actions_taken = []\n  # Define a reasonable upper bound on steps to avoid infinite loops\n  max_steps = 2000\n  # Retrieve the mapping of action names to integer IDs from the environment\n  # and store just the IDs for convenient random selection.\n  action_ids = list(env.action_specs().values())\n  # Main interaction loop: at each step select a random valid action,\n  # execute it, store it, and stop if the episode ends.\n  for _ in range(max_steps):\n      # Randomly pick an action ID from the available actions\n      act = int(np.random.choice(action_ids))\n      # Apply the action to the environment; the step method returns\n      # (reward, done, observation_dict) according to the CraftLab API.\n      _, done, _ = env.step(act)\n      # Record the action taken.\n      actions_taken.append(act)\n      # If the environment signals termination (goal reached or max steps),\n      # exit the loop early.\n      if done:\n          break\n  # Return the list of actions executed during this episode.\n  return actions_taken", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": -1}}
