{"timestamp": "2025-11-03T17:05:11.153725", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Retrieve the action mapping from the environment.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  # Expected action names; fallback to None if not present.\n  DOWN = action_map.get(\"DOWN\")\n  UP = action_map.get(\"UP\")\n  LEFT = action_map.get(\"LEFT\")\n  RIGHT = action_map.get(\"RIGHT\")\n  USE = action_map.get(\"USE\")\n\n  # Build a simple exploration pattern.  The order is not critical;\n  # we just want the agent to move around and occasionally issue a USE\n  # action (which picks up or interacts with whatever is in front).\n  pattern = [a for a in (RIGHT, DOWN, LEFT, UP, USE) if a is not None]\n\n  # Determine how many steps we are allowed to take.  The task object\n  # contains the maximum number of steps; if it is missing we default\n  # to 100 steps.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"task\", None)\n  max_steps = max_steps.steps if max_steps is not None else 100\n\n  # Generate a list of actions by cycling through the pattern until we\n  # reach the required length.\n  actions = []\n  idx = 0\n  while len(actions) < max_steps:\n      actions.append(pattern[idx % len(pattern)])\n      idx += 1\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-11-03T17:05:12.289114", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  return []", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
