{"timestamp": "2025-11-03T17:29:05.012643", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Simple random policy: keep taking random actions until the task is done or a step limit is reached.\n  actions = []\n  # Use the environment's max_steps attribute if present, otherwise fall back to a default.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 200)\n\n  for _ in range(max_steps):\n      # If the environment provides an internal termination check, respect it.\n      if hasattr(env, \"_is_done\") and env._is_done():\n          break\n\n      # Choose a random action from the five possible actions (0\u20114).\n      action = int(np.random.randint(0, 5))\n      reward, done, _ = env.step(action)\n\n      actions.append(action)\n\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": -1}}
