{"timestamp": "2025-11-03T17:34:37.952140", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Access the current CraftState from the environment\n  state = env._current_state\n\n  # Current agent position\n  x, y = state.pos\n\n  # Mapping from direction index to (dx, dy) offsets.\n  # Assuming direction indices follow the action specs:\n  # 0: DOWN, 1: UP, 2: LEFT, 3: RIGHT\n  dir_to_delta = {\n      0: (0, 1),   # DOWN\n      1: (0, -1),  # UP\n      2: (-1, 0),  # LEFT\n      3: (1, 0)    # RIGHT\n  }\n\n  # Get the delta for the requested direction; default to no movement if unknown\n  dx, dy = dir_to_delta.get(dir, (0, 0))\n\n  # Target cell coordinates\n  tx, ty = x + dx, y + dy\n\n  # Ensure the target cell is within grid bounds\n  width, height = state.grid.shape[:2]\n  if 0 <= tx < width and 0 <= ty < height:\n      # Clear any entity in the target cell by zero\u2011ing out all kind channels\n      state.grid[tx, ty, :] = 0\n\n  # This helper does not generate any high\u2011level actions itself;\n  # it directly mutates the environment, so we return an empty list.\n  return []", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
