{"timestamp": "2025-11-03T17:35:21.953027", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  import numpy as np\n\n  # Reset the environment to start a new episode and obtain the initial observation.\n  env.reset()\n\n  # Prepare a list to store the sequence of actions we will take.\n  actions = []\n\n  # Determine a reasonable upper bound on the number of steps.\n  # Use the max_steps configured in the CraftLab wrapper if available,\n  # otherwise fall back to a default limit.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 500)\n\n  # The number of possible actions is defined by the underlying CraftWorld.\n  n_actions = getattr(env.world, \"n_actions\", 5)\n\n  # Simple random policy: sample actions uniformly at random until the episode ends\n  # or we exceed the step limit.\n  for _ in range(max_steps):\n      a = int(np.random.randint(0, n_actions))\n      actions.append(a)\n\n      # Execute the action. The step method returns (reward, done, observation).\n      _, done, _ = env.step(a)\n\n      # If the task is completed (or max steps reached inside env), stop early.\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": -1}}
