{"timestamp": "2025-11-03T17:46:13.976626", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Reset the environment to start a new episode and obtain the initial observation.\n  env.reset()\n  actions = []\n\n  # Retrieve the maximum number of steps allowed for this task.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 1000)\n\n  # Main loop: keep acting until the task is completed or the step limit is reached.\n  for _ in range(max_steps):\n      # Access the underlying CraftState to inspect the world.\n      state = getattr(env, \"_current_state\", None)\n      if state is None:\n          break  # Safety check; should not happen after reset.\n\n      # If the goal has already been satisfied, stop early.\n      if env._is_done():\n          break\n\n      # Determine whether there is a grabbable entity adjacent to the agent.\n      # If so, the appropriate action is USE (action index 4).\n      use_action = None\n      for kind_idx in state.world.grabbable_indices:\n          if state.next_to(kind_idx):\n              use_action = 4  # USE\n              break\n\n      # If no adjacent grabbable item, pick a random movement action.\n      if use_action is None:\n          # Movement actions are: DOWN=0, UP=1, LEFT=2, RIGHT=3\n          use_action = np.random.randint(0, 4)\n\n      # Record and execute the chosen action.\n      actions.append(int(use_action))\n      _, done, _ = env.step(int(use_action))\n\n      # If the environment reports the episode is done, exit the loop.\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  # Return the sequence of actions taken during the episode.\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": -1}}
