{"timestamp": "2025-11-03T17:46:45.001116", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Reset the environment to start a new episode and obtain the initial observation.\n  obs = env.reset()\n  # List to record the sequence of actions taken.\n  action_sequence = []\n\n  # Retrieve the mapping from action names to integer codes.\n  action_map = env.action_specs()\n  # Extract the integer action codes in a deterministic order.\n  actions = [action_map[name] for name in sorted(action_map.keys())]\n\n  # Determine a safe upper bound for the number of steps.\n  # Prefer the environment's own max_steps attribute if it exists.\n  max_steps = getattr(env, \"max_steps\", 1000)\n\n  # Simple exhaustive policy: iterate over all possible actions each step\n  # until the task is marked as done or the step limit is reached.\n  for _ in range(max_steps):\n      for a in actions:\n          reward, done, obs = env.step(a)\n          action_sequence.append(a)\n          if done:\n              return action_sequence\n\n  # If the episode did not finish within the step budget, return whatever actions were taken.\n  return action_sequence", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": -1}}
