{"timestamp": "2025-11-03T18:17:56.242063", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  import random\n\n  # Reset the environment to start a new episode and obtain the initial observation.\n  obs = env.reset()\n  actions = []\n\n  # Retrieve the list of possible action integers from the environment.\n  possible_actions = list(env.action_specs().values())\n\n  # Define a maximum number of steps to avoid infinite loops.\n  MAX_STEPS = 1000\n\n  for _ in range(MAX_STEPS):\n      # Choose a random action (including movement and USE) as a simple policy.\n      act = random.choice(possible_actions)\n      actions.append(act)\n\n      # Apply the action to the environment.\n      reward, done, obs = env.step(act)\n\n      # If the episode has terminated (goal reached or max steps exceeded), stop.\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
