{"timestamp": "2025-11-03T18:19:43.019053", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  # Simple random policy: keep taking random actions until the task is done or a step limit is reached.\n  # Reset the environment to start a new episode.\n  observation = env.reset()\n  actions = []\n\n  # Determine the set of possible action integers.\n  try:\n      # For CraftLab, action_specs() returns a dict mapping action names to ints.\n      possible_actions = list(env.action_specs().values())\n  except Exception:\n      # Fallback: assume a fixed number of actions (e.g., 5: DOWN, UP, LEFT, RIGHT, USE).\n      possible_actions = list(range(5))\n\n  max_steps = 1000  # safety cap to avoid infinite loops\n  for _ in range(max_steps):\n      # If the environment signals completion, stop collecting actions.\n      if hasattr(env, \"_is_done\") and env._is_done():\n          break\n      # Sample a random action from the available actions.\n      action = np.random.choice(possible_actions)\n      actions.append(int(action))\n      # Apply the action; ignore reward and observation details.\n      reward, done, observation = env.step(action)\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": -1}}
