{"timestamp": "2025-11-03T18:25:47.019556", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  import numpy as np\n\n  # Initialize the environment\n  env.reset()\n  actions = []\n\n  # Obtain the list of possible action IDs from the environment\n  action_ids = list(env.action_specs().values())\n\n  # Define a generous step limit to avoid infinite loops\n  MAX_STEPS = 2000\n\n  for _ in range(MAX_STEPS):\n      # Sample a random action from the available set\n      act = int(np.random.choice(action_ids))\n\n      # Execute the action; step returns (reward, done, observation)\n      _, done, _ = env.step(act)\n\n      # Record the action taken\n      actions.append(act)\n\n      # Stop if the episode is finished (goal reached or max steps hit)\n      if done:\n          break\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": -1}}
