{"timestamp": "2025-11-03T18:31:59.120710", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  import numpy as np\n\n  # Reset the environment to start a new episode and obtain the initial observation.\n  obs = env.reset()\n  actions = []\n  done = False\n\n  # Obtain the list of possible action integers from the environment's spec.\n  # This works even if the underlying action space changes.\n  action_values = list(env.action_specs().values())\n\n  # Simple random policy: keep taking random actions until the episode ends\n  # or a safety limit on the number of steps is reached.\n  max_steps = 1000  # safety cap to avoid infinite loops\n  while not done and len(actions) < max_steps:\n      # Choose a random action from the allowed actions.\n      a = int(np.random.choice(action_values))\n      # Apply the action to the environment.\n      reward, done, obs = env.step(a)\n      # Record the action taken.\n      actions.append(a)\n\n  # Return the sequence of actions executed during the episode.\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": -1}}
