{"timestamp": "2025-11-03T18:41:08.848600", "function_name": "break_func", "function_body": "  import numpy as np\n\n  # Reset the environment to start a new episode and obtain the initial observation.\n  # The reset method returns an observation dict, but we only need the environment state.\n  env.reset()\n\n  actions = []\n  done = False\n  # Safety cap to avoid infinite loops in case the environment never signals done.\n  max_steps = 1000\n\n  # Retrieve the mapping from action names to integer IDs.\n  action_ids = list(env.action_specs().values())\n\n  while not done and len(actions) < max_steps:\n      # Choose a random valid action each step.\n      act = np.random.choice(action_ids)\n      actions.append(int(act))\n\n      # Apply the action; `step` returns (reward, done, observation).\n      _, done, _ = env.step(act)\n\n  return actions", "env_interactions": 0, "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": -1}}
